    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "At a particular time of the day, a tree casts a shadow of length $5.2\\text{ m}$ and a $30\\text{ cm}$ ruler casts a shadow of length $16\\text{ cm}$. Find the height of the tree.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$9.75\\text{ m}$",
      "worked": "The tree and ruler form similar right-angled triangles with their shadows: the sunlight makes equal corresponding angles, so the triangles are similar by AAA. Let the tree’s height be $h$ metres.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{h}{5.2}&=\\frac{30}{16}\\\\h&=5.2\\times\\frac{30}{16}\\\\h&=9.75\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
